{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands","id":332471,"title":"Mortals delving into the Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-06T13:36:16-08:00","id":332471,"title":"Mortals delving into the Shadowlands","content":"Watched about half of the film Flatliners this morning. I had an interesting thought. What happens when a mortal delves into the Shadowlands? I'm not talking about Mediums who can talk to the dead, but what they were doing in the movie or the ending of the Frighteners. What sort of effects would happen to their health or sanity? Would they be subjected to a Harrowing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:10:46-08:00","id":332490,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting subject. I'd suggest looking to Orpheus and Guildbook: Sandmen for inspiration and thoughts about this.<br /> <br /> Crossing the Shroud and travelling to the Shadowlands can be a harrowing (not Harrowing) ordeal for a mortal. The Dark Umbra is not like the material world. Emotions have a wheight and substance there, and the strong energies of death can infect a soul and take root. Mortals who go there and return should not be quite the same as before.<br /> Crossing into the Shadowlands physically requires powerful magic, and it's usually only done by Awakened mages. The Shroud is so thick these days that the deeds of Orpheus are all but impossible. Still, there are always exceptions. During certain days of the year at certain locations, the Shroud can grow dangerously thin. Giovanni vampires have access to NEcromancy rituals that may thin the shroud even further, and other works of dark, necromantic magic could have similiar effects. The poor, unfortunate soul who stumbles through one of these &quot;holes&quot; in the Shroud would find himself in a very dangerous situation. Living flesh was never ment to withstand the dark influence of Oblivion, and as a GM I would make the effects of Oblivion harsh and punishing if a body was exposed to it for any prolonged periods of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:19:09-08:00","id":332497,"title":"","content":"Well hard to say. There are groups like the Orphic Circle that do explore the Underworld but I don't know much about them as I don't have the Mediums book that talks about them. There is Orpheus which is a bit... complex given the nature of the Orpheus line. It's been a while since I've read <i>End Game</i> where they actually penetrate the Stormwall and enter the Underworld and I don't recall anything like that in the book. Then again the Projectors of Orpheus are by their nature already touched by death and would be a bit desensitized with everything they had seen before hand.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:30:06-08:00","id":332502,"title":"","content":"Interesting responses. Let's go with the spirit of the film. No supernatural influences. What sort of changes would occur when you manually cross over to the Shadowlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:34:01-08:00","id":332503,"title":"","content":"Assuming it is possible, and they do it like in the film with induced near-death experiences.. You'd technically be a Wraith, but without Passions and only your body for a Fetter.<br /> As for what changes occur, I have a rather nasty idea: Your Shadow awakens, and stays awake when you return to your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T15:06:01-08:00","id":332515,"title":"","content":"I like it. I like it a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:43:46-08:00","id":334439,"title":"","content":"From <b>Orpheus</b>\u2019 write-up of Sleepers (a type of Projector):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Sleepers receive the same sort of training that skimmers receive but lack the key physical, psychological or spiritual trait enabling skimmers to project more-or-less at will. Instead, sleepers enter special chambers reminiscent of the earliest cryogenic tanks that Orpheus used to preserve its clients in a state of near-death. Orpheus technicians replace his blood with a serum that maintains the organs' health even as they ought naturally to decay and atrophy and reduce the sleeper's core temperature to around minus 80\u00baF. Orpheus consultants refer to this process as \u201cflatlining.\u201d Once flatlined, the sleeper can project just as a skimmer does, and acts in most ways as does a ghost. His soul is lightly tethered to his body, though unlike a skimmer, he is in no danger of ghostly damage pushing its way out to his body.</span></div>Orpheus\u2019 Sleepers <i>are</i> Flatliners. And if I understand it correctly, the \u201cmultiple near-death experiences\u201d thing is more a pragmatic recruiting filter of \u201cif you\u2019ve done it before, chances are you can do it again\u201d rather than \u201cthere\u2019s something supernatural about you\u201d. Other companies (or \u201cfreelancers\u201d operating on a shoestring budget in a university\u2019s labs) may not hold to the same standards, with the likely result that prospective \u201cSleepers\u201d often end up as vegetables instead of Projecting. This, I think, would be the main difference between a professional Sleeper and a first-time Flatliner: in the latter case, there\u2019s a very real chance that your spirit will immediately Transcend or be sucked into Oblivion, scuttling any plans you might have had about Projecting. Not everyone who dies becomes a ghost. By contrast, Sleepers have already demonstrated that they have what it takes to stick around. <br /> <br /> <b>Orpheus</b> also made a few assumptions about some metaphysical changes brought about by the Sixth Great Maelstrom, such as the transformation of the Shroud into an impenetrable Stormwall (and the notion that spirits of the dead reside on this side of the Stormwall rather than on the other side of a Shroud) and the fact that Spirits get Spectre nemeses instead of Shadows; but that\u2019s inherent to the timeframe the game was set in. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m curious how Wr20 is going to handle Orpheus and its Projectors. I <i>suspect</i> that Sleepers and Skimmers will be handled just like Wraiths while they\u2019re Projecting, with all of <b>Orpheus</b>\u2019 business about Shades and Horrors being replaced by an ability to learn and use appropriate Arcanoi while Projecting. That\u2019s certainly the way I\u2019d handle it: most of the Shades and Horrors found in <b>Orpheus</b> were inspired by <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s Arcanoi, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:48:29-08:00","id":334448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=334439#post334439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m curious how Wr20 is going to handle Orpheus and its Projectors. I <i>suspect</i> that Sleepers and Skimmers will be handled just like Wraiths while they\u2019re Projecting, with all of <b>Orpheus</b>\u2019 business about Shades and Horrors being replaced by an ability to learn and use appropriate Arcanoi while Projecting. That\u2019s certainly the way I\u2019d handle it: most of the Shades and Horrors found in <b>Orpheus</b> were inspired by <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s Arcanoi, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this is the direction they take Orpheus in for Wr20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:34:47-08:00","id":334543,"title":"","content":"Yeah that would be great to see. Definitely the Orpheus treatment in Wr20 is one of the things I most want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T23:35:48-08:00","id":394548,"title":"","content":"don't euthanatoi journey to the kingdoms of the dead as their initiation? some even go tho the center of the labyrinth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T07:57:27-08:00","id":394834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if I understand it correctly, the \u201cmultiple near-death experiences\u201d thing is more a pragmatic recruiting filter of \u201cif you\u2019ve done it before, chances are you can do it again\u201d rather than \u201cthere\u2019s something supernatural about you\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> So part of the wraith &quot;Masquerade&quot; is due to the Fog - the instinctual, almost biological reaction to the presence of the dead, causing a mortal to blank out or react according to their flight/fight reflex. Humans with a higher Willpower are less subject to the Fog, but it remains there unless you desensitize the individual by making them a consort or something.<br /> <br /> Projectors, having nearly met death several times, aren't subject to that instinctual reaction because the feeling of almost dying has become normalized for them. Psychologically, they're familiar - and, on some level, <i>comfortable </i>- with the idea of dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope this is the direction they take Orpheus in for Wr20. </div> </div> </div>I kind of considered Shades to be an integral part of the <b>Orpheus</b> experience, though things may change between now and final draft time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T13:51:36-08:00","id":395325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=394834#post394834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite.<br /> <br /> So part of the wraith &quot;Masquerade&quot; is due to the Fog - the instinctual, almost biological reaction to the presence of the dead, causing a mortal to blank out or react according to their flight/fight reflex. Humans with a higher Willpower are less subject to the Fog, but it remains there unless you desensitize the individual by making them a consort or something.<br /> <br /> Projectors, having nearly met death several times, aren't subject to that instinctual reaction because the feeling of almost dying has become normalized for them. Psychologically, they're familiar - and, on some level, <i>comfortable </i>- with the idea of dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. The point is that Sleepers are suitable candidates because of the multiple near-death experiences, rather than having had multiple near-death experiences because they\u2019re suitable candidates. (Skimmers are potentially a different story in that regard, as they have a key physical, psychological or spiritual trait that lets them project more or less at will; whether they always had that trait and it was activated by their near-death experiences, or they developed it in response to their near-death experience, is an open question.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=394834#post394834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of considered Shades to be an integral part of the <b>Orpheus</b> experience, though things may change between now and final draft time.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. Really, my issue was less with that side of it than the business of Horrors vs. Arcanoi. That said, the bit about Shades was essentially giving everyone \u2014 Projectors and ghosts alike \u2014 an x-splat, where the nature of your manifestations, the powers that you are naturally inclined toward, and your general temperament are all bundled together. On the one hand, I <i>don\u2019t</i> want Projectors to be radically different from Wraiths while they\u2019re projected (that was another big part of the Orpheus experience: if a skimmer or sleeper dies while projecting, he remains more or less the same \u2014 just without a body to return to), so my thought was for <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s take on Orpheus\u2019 projectors to be more wraith-like. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I could see presenting the Shades as an optional system for Storytellers who like the notion that human souls naturally fall into broad types, leading to wraiths getting classified as poltergeists, banshees, wisps, etc., with built-in affinities for suitable Arcanoi \u2014 which in turn would lead to the Shades being a significant factor in Guild recruiting. <br /> <br /> What I <i>don\u2019t</i> want to see is \u201cyou\u2019re a projector, so you have a Shade. Oh, look; your body died, and now you\u2019re a wraith. Bye bye, Shade\u2026\u201d Almost as bad would be the notion that Orpheus\u2019 Spirits exist alongside wraiths as similar but distinct denizens of the lands of the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-06-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T17:54:18-08:00","id":395679,"title":"","content":"as for the psicological effect..oh my god, let the madness be born. i would make some kind of Fobia of Dying for the characters or fear to die. also, imagine what would happend if all your beliefs on heaven are a lie and you go to the closest thing there is to Hell. id magine that the characters would gradually loose Willpower and that some wraiths would try to pinpoint them as an Anomaly or something thats breaking Da Rules (you know, not involving in human affairs..would the wraiths have to ignore them in that case? would talk to them go against Da Rules ?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T18:31:50-08:00","id":395724,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call the Underworld Hell, its more like Purgatory sitting over the yawning maw of utter Nothingness. All things considering its not the worst place to be when you die. You want a real Hell, try the Thousand Hells.<br /> <br /> And yes, for me the biggest question regarding WtO and Orpheus, how does the Hierarchy react to the Orpheus Group and their exploration (and/or meddling) in the realm of the Dead. By their own laws they can't interfere with the Living but what do they do when the Living create companies that interfere with the Dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:25:24-08:00","id":395766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, for me the biggest question regarding WtO and Orpheus, how does the Hierarchy react to the Orpheus Group and their exploration (and/or meddling) in the realm of the Dead. By their own laws they can't interfere with the Living but what do they do when the Living create companies that interfere with the Dead? </div> </div> </div>Here is the preamble of the Dictum Mortuum...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I, Charon, Emperor of Stygia, by the power of the words of the Lady of Fate, do hereby set these laws down that they may serve to bring order between this world and the former;(1) that no wraith under any circumstances for any reason is to penetrate the barrier that divideth the Land of the Dead from the Land of the Quick;(2) to engage in congress with those that have not yet passed over, or speak to the Quick of events yet to come;(3) or in any way, shape, or form harass, threaten injure or otherwise compel those in the Land of the Quick to do the bidding of those in the Land of the Dead;(4) or import upon those in the Land of the Quick any desire or compunction to take a life, be it their own or that of another, in order to effect the passing over of one or more to the Land of the Dead, be they friend or foe, parent, child or lover... </div> </div> </div> (ennumeration mine)<br /> <br /> If you take a strict reading of this...<br /> <br /> 1)A member of Orpheus Group who has crossed over into the Land of the Dead is already there, and so interacting with that person does not cross the shroud.<br /> 2)If you follow this by spirit, then a member of Orpheus Group who is in the Shadowlands should not be spoken with at all. One could argue, however, that a member of Orpheus Group who is in the shadowlands has &quot;passed over&quot; and thus can be interacted with freely.<br /> 3)Note the word &quot;in&quot; the Land of the Quick. not &quot;of&quot;. <br /> 4)Again, the use of the word &quot;in&quot;. Also can be taken as a forbiddance against helping Orpheus Group to cross over into the Shadowlands...<br /> <br /> It's also said (p. 52) that the Code is continually updated, but most Shadowland agents don't have the time or energy to read it, let alone enforce it, and simply concentrate on keeping the peace. It's possible that Stygia could declare Orpheus Group to be an enemy of the state and a threat to the Dictum Mortuum, or it could be simply treated as a local issue and left to the individual Necropoli to sort out. I guess it depends on how big a threat Orpheus is to Stygia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T13:15:31-08:00","id":396688,"title":"","content":"I've found The Benandanti, The Unhooded, when I was making my Wraith for the Great War pbp. Not only they are the Flatliners, there are subfactions within the group. The Risorgeritori (Resurrectionists), Damnati (Damned/Blackshirts), and Redentori (Redeemers). They're Italian, membership begins at birth literally and been instructed how to crossover and venture through the Shadowlands since childhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T01:24:19-08:00","id":427522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=394548#post394548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">don't euthanatoi journey to the kingdoms of the dead as their initiation? some even go tho the center of the labyrinth</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but is it more of a &quot;Dip&quot; then a plunge for the initiation, and it usually involves the initiate dying in some fashion. It's to show the initiate that yes there is an afterlife and that they have a duty to the wheel...ect..ect... Think of the bathtub scene from Constantine. <br /> <br /> Adepts and Masters have been known to journey to the lands of the dead for personal reasons but never for a vacation. They are the lands of the dead after all....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T09:06:58-08:00","id":427778,"title":"","content":"I can soooooo imagine Voormas under a beach umbrella, sitting on a lounge chair (both made of the bones and skin of his enemies) on the shore of the Sea of Shadows sipping a screaming Moliated wraith (which of course, he killed) from a soulsteel cup (ditto) and calling up some current Harrowings out of the Tempest. To watch them &quot;frolic&quot;. Like people watch dolphins playing....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:11:30-08:00","id":427871,"title":"","content":"It seems like the most interesting effect of any skinlander making contact with the Shadowlands, by any means, would be attracting the attention of its denizens -- who would invariably see the visitor as a possible collaborator and/or threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T11:20:11-08:00","id":427882,"title":"","content":"So, no comments on the Benandanti?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T02:18:03-08:00","id":428884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=427778#post427778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can soooooo imagine Voormas under a beach umbrella, sitting on a lounge chair (both made of the bones and skin of his enemies) on the shore of the Sea of Shadows sipping a screaming Moliated wraith (which of course, he killed) from a soulsteel cup (ditto) and calling up some current Harrowings out of the Tempest. To watch them &quot;frolic&quot;. Like people watch dolphins playing....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, ok anyone besides Voormas, the dude is president of club Jhor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:06:41-07:00","id":434066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1)A member of Orpheus Group who has crossed over into the Land of the Dead is already there, and so interacting with that person does not cross the shroud.<br /> 2)If you follow this by spirit, then a member of Orpheus Group who is in the Shadowlands should not be spoken with at all. One could argue, however, that a member of Orpheus Group who is in the shadowlands has &quot;passed over&quot; and thus can be interacted with freely.<br /> 3)Note the word &quot;in&quot; the Land of the Quick. not &quot;of&quot;.<br /> 4)Again, the use of the word &quot;in&quot;. Also can be taken as a forbiddance against helping Orpheus Group to cross over into the Shadowlands... </div> </div> </div>The interaction between the Dictum Mortuum is something Rich and I discussed a lot while I was writing my chapter, because even a charitable reading of the Dictum is pretty clear about interactions with Orpheus agents being a violation. The big saving grace to a tolerant Anachreon is that Charon instituted the Dictum to stop the dead from gaining power from and over the living. He never seriously expected the living to come to the lands of the dead. Orpheus' existence is largely without precedent.<br /> <br /> It violates the letter of the law, but whether it violates the spirit - or whether the spirit should even matter in a world with the Orpheus Group - is up for debate, and thus grist for the drama mill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:10:01-07:00","id":435452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=434066#post434066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The interaction between the Dictum Mortuum is something Rich and I discussed a lot while I was writing my chapter, because even a charitable reading of the Dictum is pretty clear about interactions with Orpheus agents being a violation. The big saving grace to a tolerant Anachreon is that Charon instituted the Dictum to stop the dead from gaining power from and over the living. He never seriously expected the living to come to the lands of the dead. Orpheus' existence is largely without precedent.<br /> <br /> It violates the letter of the law, but whether it violates the spirit - or whether the spirit should even matter in a world with the Orpheus Group - is up for debate, and thus grist for the drama mill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it will definitely be interesting to see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:12:27-07:00","id":435455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=427882#post427882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, no comments on the Benandanti?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the blurb in the 2e Wraith book, I haven't read much about them, but they could make really interesting NPC's. Beyond being a secretive group of mystics, I don't really know much about them to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:09:13-07:00","id":441629,"title":"","content":"There's more in The Great War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:54:06-07:00","id":442073,"title":"","content":"The most notable thing about them is that they beat Orpheus to the punch by a significant margin on the whole \u201cProjectors\u201d thing: each of them is effectively a Skimmer, made that way by an occult rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:00:48-07:00","id":442544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=442073#post442073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most notable thing about them is that they beat Orpheus to the punch by a significant margin on the whole \u201cProjectors\u201d thing: each of them is effectively a Skimmer, made that way by an occult rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a weird little quirk of their birth. Which seems much more prevalent in their families than normal. Selective pressure favoring a mutation the point of it becoming an adaptation? Does being able to walk the Shadowlands actually benefit the Benendatti in some way, evolutionarily speaking? If so, what are they getting out of it? (Maybe the WoD just selects for humans to become supernatural... that's definitely more advantageous than &quot;keep your head down and hope IT goes away&quot;. Pretty much all the time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:44:55-07:00","id":444183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332471-mortals-delving-into-the-shadowlands?p=442073#post442073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most notable thing about them is that they beat Orpheus to the punch by a significant margin on the whole \u201cProjectors\u201d thing: each of them is effectively a Skimmer, made that way by an occult rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most notable thing about Orpheus wasn't the development of skimming, it was the scientific development of skimming <i>and </i>sleeper technology. We don't need no caul, I ain't afraid of no ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}